      "message": "Use the default branch's config on pull requests from authors without write access (#2088)\n\n* Use the default branch's config on pull requests from authors without write access\n\nWhen a pull request's author does not have write access and it targets a branch\nother than the default one, the config that the action restores now comes from\nthe base_branch input or the default branch instead of the pull request's base.\nThe base is still fetched so that the two can be compared.\n\nFetch and check out the config branch by its full ref name, so that a tag of the\nsame name or a narrow refspec can't leave the session without config.\n\nDocument that pr-N holds a fork's commits and should stay out of CI that holds\nsecrets.\n\nCo-authored-by: mhegazy <mhegazy@anthropic.com>\n\n* Keep the other branch's config out of commits and the base comparable\n\nThe commit wrapper leaves out files that the action took from a branch other than\nthe pull request's base. HEAD's history is fetched again if fetching the config\nbranch cut it, and a base branch that can't be fetched fails the run as before.\nA bot's pull request into a pr-N branch no longer takes its config from it.\n\nCo-authored-by: mhegazy <mhegazy@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
